    <exercise number="306" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>For $$f(x) = \frac{P(x)}{Q(x)}$$ to have an asymptote at $$y = 2$$ then the polynomials $$P(x)$$ and $$Q(x)$$ must have what relation?</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="307" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>For $$f(x) = \frac{P(x)}{Q(x)}$$ to have an asymptote at $$x = 0,$$ then the polynomials $$P(x)$$ and $$Q(x).$$ must have what relation?</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$P ( 0 ) \ne 0 and Q ( 0 ) = 0 P ( 0 ) \ne 0 and Q ( 0 ) = 0$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="308" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>If $$f^{\prime}(x)$$ has asymptotes at $$y = 3$$ and $$x = 1,$$ then $$f(x)$$ has what asymptotes?</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="309" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Both $$f(x) = \frac{1}{\left( {x - 1} \right)}$$ and $$g(x) = \frac{1}{\left( {x - 1} \right)^{2}}$$ have asymptotes at $$x = 1$$ and $$y = 0.$$ What is the most obvious difference between these two functions?</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$lim x \to 1 - f ( x ) = -\infty and lim x \to 1 - g ( x ) = \infty lim x \to 1 - f ( x ) = -\infty and lim x \to 1 - g ( x ) = \infty$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
